# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value for your environment.
# .env.local is gitignored — never commit real URLs or credentials.

# ── Data source (pick one) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option 1: Google Sheets published as CSV
#   File → Share → Publish to web → Sheet (public tab only) → CSV
#   The published tab should contain only fuzzed coordinates and public fields.
# VITE_DATA_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/SHEET_ID/pub?output=csv&gid=SHEET_GID

# Option 2: Static CSV served alongside the app
#   Place your CSV in the public/ directory and reference it by path.
# VITE_DATA_URL=/data.csv

# Set to 1 if your CSV has two header rows (e.g. the original Map-data export).
# Default: 0 (single header row — standard Google Sheets published CSV format).
# VITE_DATA_SKIP_ROWS=1

# When VITE_DATA_URL is not set, the app uses the bundled static dataset
# (src/data/data-fuzzed.ts) compiled into the build at deploy time.
